:["The Kretschmann scalar $K$ and the Ricci scalar $R$ of the topological star against $r$ ($r_S = 3r_B/4$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, $\\phi$, and $y$, beside the Einstein metric of four dimensions it reduces to. On the bubble $r = r_B$, where the circle $y$ closes to a point, $K$ is greatest and finite, $291/64r_B^4 = 4.547/r_B^4$, and it falls at every $r$. In four dimensions the bubble is a naked singularity, and the Einstein metric's $K$ grows there without bound, as $15/1024r_B(r - r_B)^3$. It crosses the star's $K$ once, at $r = 2.891\\,r_B$, and lies below it outside. Far out the star's $K$ falls off as $12(r_S^2 + r_Sr_B + r_B^2)/r^6$, and the Einstein metric's as $3(2r_S + r_B)^2/r^6$, Schwarzschild's of the same mass.","$R = r_Sr_B/2r^4$ is positive at every $r$ and greatest on the bubble, $3/8r_B^2 = 0.375/r_B^2$. The Einstein metric's $R$ grows there without bound, as $3/32\\sqrt{r_B}(r - r_B)^{3/2}$, and lies above the star's at every $r$. Far out each $R$ falls off as $3r_B^2/8r^4$."],"ricci_sentences":[[1,0],[1,1],[1,2]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of the topological star against $r$ ($r_S = 3r_B/4$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, $\\phi$, and $y$, beside the Einstein metric of four dimensions it reduces to.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_B^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-4}$ to $10^{4}$ and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as the Einstein metric's $K$ does inside $r = 1.011\\,r_B$.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","the Einstein metric of four dimensions it reduces to"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R$ of the topological star against $r$ ($r_S = 3r_B/4$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, $\\phi$, and $y$, beside the Einstein metric of four dimensions it reduces to.","clip":"We draw $R\\,r_B^2$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-4}$ to $10^{2}$ and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as the Einstein metric's $R$ does inside $r = 1.010\\,r_B$.","legend":[["line","R","$R$, the Ricci scalar"],["line","reference","the Einstein metric of four dimensions it reduces to"]]}},"settings":"$r_B = 1$, the unit of every length, and $r_S = 3r_B/4$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_B^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-4}$ to $10^{4}$ and $R\\,r_B^2$ on one from $10^{-4}$ to $10^{2}$, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as the Einstein metric's $K$ does inside $r = 1.011\\,r_B$ and its $R$ inside $r = 1.010\\,r_B$."},{"id":"string","label":"The black string","system":"eddington_finkelstein_ingoing","kind":"line","x":{"name":"$r/r_S$","from":0.75,"to":4.75,"ticks":[{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"},{"at":3.0,"label":"$3$"},{"at":4.0,"label":"$4$"}]},"panels":[{"id":"K","name":"$K\\,r_S^4$","aspect":2,"scale":{"kind":"log","from":0.0001,"to":10000.0},"ticks":[{"at":0.0001,"label":"$10^{-4}$"},{"at":0.01,"label":"$10^{-2}$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$10^{0}$"},{"at":100.0,"label":"$10^{2}$"},{"at":10000.0,"label":"$10^{4}$"}]},{"id":"R","name":"$R\\,r_S^2$","aspect":2,"scale":{"kind":"symlog","from":-100.0,"to":100.0,"linear":0.0001},"ticks":[{"at":-100.0,"label":"$-10^{2}$"},{"at":-1.0,"label":"$-10^{0}$"},{"at":-0.01,"label":"$-10^{-2}$"},{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.01,"label":"$10^{-2}$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$10^{0}$"},{"at":100.0,"label":"$10^{2}$"}]}],"curves":[{"panel":"K","class":"reference","metric":"topological_star","system":"einstein","scalar":"kretschmann","coordinate":"r","params":{"r_S":1.0,"r_B":0.75},"points":[[0.753,1322052.8511454882],[0.756,170748.24357506016],[0.76,38767.251245228916],[0.766,10297.47462670835],[0.773,3856.470931292048],[0.778,2311.402755026171],[0.783,1526.7508858176077],[0.789,1014.3989225759361],[0.795,722.2113901100554],[0.803,495.4515718188301],[0.8109999999999999,361.7726048032381],[0.8200000000000001,267.9213552763311],[0.83,201.43093520851156],[0.842,150.23835959679522],[0.855,114.29641578444644],[0.87,86.94082615171693],[0.886,67.37364545538591],[0.9